  "$id": "duel-rules-4",
  "title": "duel-sim-3 issued rules snapshot with the chase / retreat block",
  "description": "duel-rules-3 plus the fight-chase-1 chase / retreat rules (DECISIONS #72.65; Contract-Change duel-rules-4-1, Pak 2026-10-22). Every duel-rules-3 key, unit and the fighter rows are unchanged; the required `chase` block carries the ten chase numbers. The core is the same duel-sim-3 core: a duel-rules-3 snapshot (no block) runs today's core byte for byte; a duel-rules-4 snapshot runs the chase rules, whose state bytes append ASCII 'fight-chase-1', the ten chase values and per side (0, 1) the int32 values tagged, retreatStart, retreatReadyAt, chasedAt, drainAcc, escapedThisRetreat, caught, retreats, ringStops, ringStopTick after the roster members. New events (not hashed): 23 Retreat, 24 Caught, 25 RingStop, 26 ChaseEnd; deny code 13 RetreatCooldown. Canonical hash: SHA-256 over ASCII 'duel-rules-4', then every rules value as int32 little-endian in FightRules.GlobalKeys order, then every chase value as int32 little-endian in FightChaseRules.Keys order, then the fighter count (int32), then per fighter in array order: int32 id length + ASCII id + every value in FightFighterDef.Keys order. JSON key order is not significant; the hash order is. Not an authorization: the host settles only from its own replay (hard rule 1). Generated by Tools/FightCoreCold/gen_rules_schema.py.",
